# Bash scripts must always check out with LF line endings. With core.autocrlf
# enabled on Windows, a .sh checked out as CRLF fails on Linux ("bad
# interpreter" / stray \r), so enforce LF regardless of platform settings.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Bash entry points must remain executable from Linux-managed or Windows-managed
# checkouts. The executable bit is tracked in the git index (mode 100755); keep
# it set for the launcher and the desktop manager.

# Release packaging: keep development-only material OUT of `git archive` output
# (GitHub release tarballs and the "Download ZIP" button use git archive). These
# files remain fully present in the repository and in any `git clone` — this
# only trims the archived release download so the official package is clean.
# Regression tests are preserved in the repository for future maintenance.
/tests export-ignore
/docs/superpowers export-ignore
/docs/w7_vmware_acceptance_checklist.md export-ignore
